ast of Mayotte in the Comoros archipelago.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzata"><span class="enc-name">Dzata</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Dzata is the site of the stone-walled capital of the Venda kingdom in the Nzhelele valley of Limpopo province, South Africa, traditionally founded by the Singo dynasty…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzhengutai"><span class="enc-name">Dzhengutai</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Dzhengutai is a village in the Buynaksky district of Dagestan, in Russia's North Caucasus, in the foothills between the Kumyk plain and the Avar mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzibanche"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/dzibanche.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dzibanche</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Dzibanche is a Maya archaeological site in southern Quintana Roo, Mexico, occupied from the late Preclassic period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzud"><span class="enc-name">Dzud</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Dzud is a Mongolian term for a catastrophic winter, when heavy snow, ice or extreme cold prevents livestock from grazing and causes mass deaths of animals.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzungar-genocide"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/dzungar-genocide.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dzungar genocide</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dzungar genocide was the mass killing of the Dzungar Oirat Mongols by Qing forces in 1755–1757 under the Qianlong Emperor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/dzungaria.jpg" alt="" loading="la